//? Title: Factorized video:complete R(2+1)D and P3D tensor fits
//? Subtitle: Tensor computations, explicit checks and reproducible local figures
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Original KTH clips feed full-depth spatial/temporal factorized residual networks. Visible Adam loops,paired BN checkpoints,all residual endpoints and every held-out/control result distinguish computation checks from limited action accuracy.
)
\toc

Source example: `examples/cpp/source/nn/1_convolutional_neural_networks/1.10_3d_and_video_convolutions/factorized_video.cpp`.

> The method

Preserve both full block sequences and source symmetric borders/P3D mixtures. Use explicit tensor Adam for each compact network,update moving BN only in fitting forwards,select paired checkpoints on validation,and restore RGB-only inference before complete held-out comparisons.

The editable concept diagram is `diagrams/factorized_video_concept.tikz`. Regeneration uses
LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, plus dvisvgm; exports use the saved SVG.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/factorized_video_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/factorized_video_concept.tikz > build/factorized_video_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/factorized_video_concept.svg build/factorized_video_concept.dvi > build/factorized_video_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered local concept diagram.\n'
```
