> Genuine annotated video,with the same original source split

Use the same original KTH data as C3D:boxing0/handclapping1/handwaving2,
scenario1,people1..4fit/5validation/6test,first two annotated segments per video.
Each segment contributes16unique actual frames evenly spaced over its bounds.
Tensor Float32 legacy bilinear resize32px and/255 follow codec-only FFmpeg
decoding. Original AVI/annotation bytes come from mirror revision
7076149bdbeff8d70003a68d6291fd080db44683 while the KTH server is unavailable.
All source hashes,frame identities,people and segments remain in the manifest.

```{cpp, flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  const std::filesystem::path cache = dm::datasets::data_home();
  dm::datasets::prepare_example_data("video", (cache / "action_video").string());
}
