> Verification and limits

Five native tests cover all530independent factor/kernel/input finite differences,
both full-reference-size graphs and all learned gradients/BN state inventories,
explicit state mutation/inference immutability,and symmetric stride/invalid
contracts. Shared video tests independently check every1769472source pixel,
reference feature and score. Every public example and original three-epoch
workflow passes. Both select epoch2:validation NLL1.099605/1.095704.
Held-out R(2+1)D accuracy.50/NLL1.094525,recalls1/0/.5;P3D accuracy1/3/
NLL1.122472,recalls0/0/1. Both miss every handclapping example and remain
below motion1NN accuracy2/3. The initial P3D held-out NLL8386.22 is retained.
This short random-initialized custom split and adaptation
of BN state do not reproduce pretrained Kinetics/Sports1M results.

> Conclusion

Both full-depth tensor graphs and their independent derivatives pass,while the compact short fits remain below the motion reference on the six held-out clips. Explicit BN state and complete errors prevent large initialization-loss changes from being mistaken for benchmark performance.

